{"author":{"id":"dec876858d28babbadcead4137861bf586626b8518cbce9c5f4fc52ac3b424b8"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1795256880,"nonce":"CmPjQWdjclO6UkIbtPoL1ZXuig8=","message":"Progress, 2026-11-21 (uncommitted).\n\nMeasure: instructions retired by `cn_demo_costs` with `COSTS_NO_TRACE=1 COSTS_CALENDAR=\u003cn\u003e COSTS_CALENDAR_PHASE=turn COSTS_CALENDAR_FRAMES=12 COSTS_CALENDAR_DT=8 COSTS_ASYNC=1`, run for 61 cycles minus a run of 1, over 720 frames. a19f0b84: 36.4 to 36.7M per frame. Working tree: 28.4 to 28.6M. Runs alternated, three each.\n\nDone\n- Staging belt takes writes up to 8 MiB (the per-frame text upload was over the old 256 KiB limit).\n- CSS layout pass scoped to what a frame's updates can change (`layout_scope.rs`); in that pass, one style read and write per node, and `#id` rules and `overflow: scroll` physics looked up for the scoped nodes only (the physics scan cloned every node's taffy `Style`).\n- Region reconcile re-mints stable ids under the region's container only (`stable_ids.rs`). Checked against the whole-tree walk on every reconcile of a 12-turn run: identical maps.\n- Opacity groups without effects or a named output use the rounded texture pool; the fading month grids changed size every frame at the window edge and created two textures a frame.\n- All 184 recorder snapshots byte-identical to a19f0b84.\n\nWhere the rest is, per 12-turn run (144 frames): 95 on rows, 23 full for the structural frames of the turns (insert the new month, remove the old), 26 full because a page holding an SVG is a static binding (ac72bd5). The structural frames are the bulk of the remaining cost: reconcile and build of 42 cells, compute_layout, then a full paint walk, element collection and overlay draw of the whole page.\n\nNot taken: dropping the straighten pass for plain groups (needs the composite shader to take premultiplied input, a uniform change, about 2% of samples).","files":null}]}